diff --git a/runtime/sdk/ov/README.md b/runtime/sdk/ov/README.md
index 1ef63f4..2e19d5d 100644
--- a/runtime/sdk/ov/README.md
+++ b/runtime/sdk/ov/README.md
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@ Replacements of `nn::*` functions by name: system, input, audio, video, graphics
 
 | File | What it is |
 |---|---|
+| `display_version.c`, `display_version.h` | Shared GetDisplayVersion payload: formats a local 16-byte result and publishes once, through checked HLE copying when selected or native memcpy by default; used by ov_oe2.c and the PS5 integration diagnostic |
 | `ov_system.c` | Accounts, applets, time, system fonts, etc. |
 | `ov_input.c`, `ov_media.c`, `ov_gfx.c`, `ov_zstd.c` | Input, Opus, the SDK's graphics (`nv::InitializeGraphics(0, 0)` is valid on Switch 2; `nv::InitCheck`), native zstd |
 | `ov_codec.c` | MKW's video: the `nn::codec` video API (VP9 with libvpx, decoded in `Submit`) and the `nn::syncpt` events as the game's `SystemEvent` |
@@ -15,3 +16,15 @@ Replacements of `nn::*` functions by name: system, input, audio, video, graphics
 | `ov_lanaddr.c` | MKW's own: the address and mask `nifm` reports in LAN mode, chosen from the host's interfaces (or `MKW_LAN_IP`) |
 | `ov_socket.c` | MKW's own: `nn::socket` as main's network-down stub by default; with `MKW_LAN=1`, over the host's sockets (datagrams, poll, eventfd), with the console's FreeBSD sockaddr, options and flags: the base of LAN play. Bind and SendTo take local network addresses only (private, link-local, multicast, broadcast), so LAN play cannot reach the internet. LAN tested on Linux only; on Windows it compiles, with ICMP resets off on datagram sockets and no eventfd (only gRPC, online, calls it) |
 | `ov_time2.c` | MKW's own: the `nn::time` that totk-pc-recomp does not replace (exact network clock, host time zone, instant clock correction) |
+
+For the PS5 build, socket errors map from native FreeBSD numbering to the
+guest's Linux errno values and IPv4 input includes the native sockaddr length.
+Linux-only EventFd explicitly returns ENOSYS on PS5, as on Windows, rather than
+requiring eventfd headers. The upstream network-down default is unchanged; PS5
+LAN operation has not been validated.
+
+On PS5, native one-shot Zstd decoding publishes a private output through checked HLE copying after thawing the actual result, avoiding stores into sparse guest holes and recording dirty pages. Input/dictionaries are committed before native reads. Streaming retains its existing stable output/history address.
+
+PS5 streaming Zstd prepares and validates its stable output window before native writes. A checked self-copy records actual output pages without relocating the history dictionary between blocks.
+
+PS5 buffer-less streaming bounds each native call and its preparation to Zstd’s maximum 128 KiB block, retaining contiguous history. Slow blocks report separate prepare/native/publish times; this avoids repeatedly preparing the entire remaining frame.
